WEBVTT

00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:05.690
Who hasn't recorded a script at some point in their life?

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.690
That is why we have created Table Read Tools,

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:15.690
a new way of looking at your scripts.

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:23.530
First of all, we assign an image to each character.

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:37.290
Then you arrange them by importance.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:42.190
That's good.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:46.290
Then we go to locations

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:48.690
and add the locations.

00:00:53.290 --> 00:00:55.290
Here is one.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.850
And the next one.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.960
And once you have everything ready, we move to the conversation module.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:13.960
From now on, you can see your scripts as if they were a chat conversation.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:21.960
It shows you the character who is speaking and the script time elapsed.

00:01:22.960 --> 00:01:25.960
Or you can view it as a script reading.

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.800
You see the space where the scene takes place and then

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:35.800
Let the magic happen by itself.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:40.800
The dialogues automatically move from one character to another

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.800
with an approximate calculation of the time needed for someone to read them.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:54.800
You can run it automatically or move forward manually.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:10.000
You can export the photographs to apply them to other projects if you have the same actors

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:15.120
And that's it, a new way of looking at your scripts.
